    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Three things, kept separate from the confirmed 41018 so you know what is a read and what is not.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The laptop password.</b> The login window, the masked field and the happy-face avatar are all clearly visible, but the characters are hidden by the mask and the game never echoes them. The Morse paper gives four groups (U, P, E, S) and that is where we would start, but we have not seen the string accepted, so it is not printed as an answer.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. The safe combination.</b> The dial is legible — 0 to 90 in tens, nine ticks between — and the recording turns it for the best part of a minute, but the door never opens inside the footage we could extract. No combination is given here.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. The exit and the closing sequence.</b> The run used for this page was reconstructed from a partly downloaded file: the last seconds, where the door opens and the level ends, are not in it. We therefore cannot show you the exit frame or a completion card for Workshop, and this page does not claim a reward figure for it.
